{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880382",
      "title": "More Custom Composition Functions",
      "lectureOrder": 317,
      "videoOrder": 283,
      "sourceHash": "5718c5cfa628a3755c093419877359c219440793a13ca0deb38ac368d31e014f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 5.2,
          "en": "So this is how you can reuse functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.2,
          "end": 8.92,
          "en": "across components when using the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.92,
          "end": 11.83,
          "en": "Now, we can do more than what we're doing thus far.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.83,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "For example, we can of course still also",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 17.6,
          "en": "setup other things in setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.6,
          "end": 21.58,
          "en": "We're not limited to just using our reuse logic here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.58,
          "end": 24.03,
          "en": "We could again import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.03,
          "end": 28.56,
          "en": "ref here, from vue. If we had some other data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.56,
          "end": 32.24,
          "en": "that should be changeable, and create our extra ref here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.24,
          "end": 36.35,
          "en": "like the alertTitle, which could be a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.35,
          "end": 40.033,
          "en": "with a starting value of Delete User?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.76,
          "end": 44.21,
          "en": "And here theoretically, I don't need a ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.21,
          "end": 47.41,
          "en": "because I won't add any logic to ever change this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 47.41,
          "end": 48.98,
          "en": "But I wanna show you that you could,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.98,
          "end": 51.17,
          "en": "of course, have extra refs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.17,
          "end": 53.8,
          "en": "as well as computed properties and watchers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.8,
          "end": 56.25,
          "en": "and anything else you can use in the setup function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.25,
          "end": 59.593,
          "en": "no matter if you are using a custom hook or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 62.15,
          "en": "But with that I can for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.15,
          "end": 64.31,
          "en": "also expose my alertTitle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.65,
          "end": 69.25,
          "en": "here, with the return statement to my template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.25,
          "end": 73.373,
          "en": "and bind the title here, to alertTitle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.776,
          "end": 76.21000000000001,
          "en": "But we can absolutely do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 76.21000000000001,
          "end": 78.3,
          "en": "And this is kind of a similar thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.3,
          "end": 81.12,
          "en": "to what I did before with the mixins.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.12,
          "end": 83.15,
          "en": "There, the mixin was automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.15,
          "end": 85.07,
          "en": "merged with your other options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.07,
          "end": 88.01,
          "en": "Here, we kind of manually merge it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.01,
          "end": 91.4,
          "en": "by simply doing one thing with our custom hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.4,
          "end": 94.713,
          "en": "and doing other things in the rest of our setup function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.05,
          "end": 98.65,
          "en": "Now, our custom hook is also able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.65,
          "end": 100.8,
          "en": "to receive arguments by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.8,
          "end": 105.69,
          "en": "here I got a custom hook function, which returns something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.69,
          "end": 109.05,
          "en": "and your hooks will typically always return something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.05,
          "end": 111.4,
          "en": "because you wanna do stuff into hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.4,
          "end": 114.6,
          "en": "which then can still be exposed to your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.6,
          "end": 117.72,
          "en": "And for that, your hook needs to make these things available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.72,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "to the setup method where it's getting called,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 124.34,
          "en": "but your hooks can also take arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.34,
          "end": 127.39,
          "en": "For example, let's say for Delete User,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.39,
          "end": 129.3,
          "en": "the default starting value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.3,
          "end": 132.76,
          "en": "for alertIsVisible should be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.76,
          "end": 135.42,
          "en": "So that by default, the alert is opened.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 138.56,
          "en": "This might not make much sense from an app perspective,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 138.56,
          "end": 140.57999999999998,
          "en": "but it's a great practice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.57999999999998,
          "end": 143.73,
          "en": "With mixins, this was kind of tricky.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 143.73,
          "end": 147.12,
          "en": "With hooks, it's easy. It's your own function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.12,
          "end": 149.85,
          "en": "So of course, useAlert may accept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.85,
          "end": 152.72,
          "en": "as many parameters as you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.72,
          "end": 155.37,
          "en": "For example, startingVisibility.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 156.5,
          "end": 158.31,
          "en": "The name of course is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.31,
          "end": 160.64,
          "en": "You can even assign a default value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.64,
          "end": 163,
          "en": "let's say false, so that you don't have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163,
          "end": 166.59300000000002,
          "en": "to pass in a value for this parameter when coding useAlert.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 170.68,
          "en": "This is a modern JavaScript feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.68,
          "end": 172.573,
          "en": "default parameter values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.57,
          "end": 176.24,
          "en": "But now we can use this and assign this here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.24,
          "end": 178.543,
          "en": "to our ref as a starting value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.55,
          "end": 181.57,
          "en": "And now since we have a default value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.57,
          "end": 184.173,
          "en": "we can still code useAlert as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 185.09,
          "end": 186.71,
          "en": "but we can also code it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.71,
          "end": 190.1,
          "en": "and pass an extra argument in, for this parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 190.1,
          "end": 192.47,
          "en": "So pass in true as a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.47,
          "end": 196.03,
          "en": "for this parameter instead of Delete User.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.03,
          "end": 198.34,
          "en": "And as a result, if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.34,
          "end": 201.27,
          "en": "we start with the model opened",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.27,
          "end": 203.623,
          "en": "for the Delete User component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.5,
          "end": 208.2,
          "en": "because of that different argument I passed in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 208.2,
          "end": 211.48,
          "en": "So your custom hooks are really flexible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.48,
          "end": 214.34,
          "en": "you can accept any arguments you might need,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.34,
          "end": 217.84,
          "en": "and you can use all the Composition API features in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 217.84,
          "end": 219.79,
          "en": "do whatever that hook needs to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 219.79,
          "end": 222.99,
          "en": "and then return to the component where you wanna",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.99,
          "end": 226.34300000000002,
          "en": "use the hook, what that hook should expose to the component.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
